WEBVTT

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:07.770
Edison: Cubik Galoit.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:10.450
Da Vinci: Ana Gram.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:13.840
Galileo: Gammon Sakanoue.

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:20.350
We were unable to separate them
from Kaito Daimon's side.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.200
Our apologies.

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:32.840
The plan is going well.

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:35.680
The next target is...

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:38.470
Kaito Daimon?

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:40.590
Uh, but...

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:42.460
Wasn't the plan to separate

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:45.230
Kaito Daimon from his
friends, make him alone?

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:48.940
We shall steal "eternity" from his heart.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:50.660
Eternity?

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:52.440
Bishop?

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:56.510
Kaito Daimon has already
returned to Japan.

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:59.200
As planned, shall we...

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:00.990
Yes, that will do.

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:10.940
Dammit, what's going on, old man?!

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:14.470
Today, for once, I'm
gonna get some answers...

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:17.970
Damn! Where the hell did he go?

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:19.930
I don't know.

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:22.050
Upperclassman Jikukawa?

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:24.510
You don't know?

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:26.480
It's causing me some distress.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.830
Kimi no nounai e to shinnyuu
Gonna infiltrate your brain

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:52.630
Nemutteru suki ni baby, open the gate
While you're sleeping, baby, open the gate

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:54.420
Fukuzatsusugi security
Too-complicated security

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:57.170
Kakusareru to abakitakunaru
When something's hidden, it makes me want to expose it

00:01:57.170 --> 00:02:01.680
Barabara ni chirabatte iru password o hiroiatsume
I'll gather up those loose, scattered passwords

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:06.390
Kakushin ni sematte yuku, sono shoutai o misete
And approach the core, so show me that true form

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:08.600
Kantan ni clear dekinai
I can't clear it easily

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:11.270
Saki nante motto yomenai
Can read what lies ahead even less

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:13.270
Kaidoku fukanou smile
A smile that can't be deciphered

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:15.570
Kiken na puzzle
A dangerous puzzle

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:17.530
Lock sareteta door aru nara
If there's a door that's been locked

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:20.320
Zutto tataite miru beki, kaza-ana hiraku wa
You must keep striking it, a crack will open

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:24.870
Eien ni hodokenai nazo nanka wa nai
No mystery remains unsolved forever

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:27.120
Makiokosu, it's a supernova!
It's forming, it's a supernova!

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:31.790
Tobikiri shigekiteki na hirameki o agemashou
I will give you thoroughly stimulating insight

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:34.040
Misskey-misskey la-tu-ma

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:36.380
Yume no naka, it's a supernova!
In the middle of a dream, it's a supernova!

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:39.010
Watashi wa, sou, brain diver
I am, yes, a brain diver

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:44.890
Kimi ga sagashimotometeru kotae ni nareru made
Until I become familiar with the answer you seek

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:50.560
Brain diver

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:55.360
Brain diver

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:03.950
The Truth

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:10.750
The principal went missing?

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:14.600
Yes, while we were overseas.

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:18.550
At a time like this? I
wonder what happened?

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:20.800
Maybe it was the POG.

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:22.630
You mean they kidnapped him?

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:24.090
Like they did me?

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:25.140
Even if they did...

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:28.190
We won't be taken out that easily.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:32.160
Baro-Baro and Souji knew

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:35.360
about Phi-Brain and the Puzzle of God.

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:45.250
Well, all we can do now
is have faith and wait.

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:56.040
Yeah, but still...

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:58.210
You really don't have any ideas?

00:03:58.610 --> 00:04:00.350
Why the hell would I?

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:04.680
But he's the guy who took you in
and raised you, right?

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:06.640
I told you:

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:09.380
He had me study abroad in
England the whole time,

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:11.430
and when he finally brought
me back, it was to here.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:15.480
Aside from the fact that
he knew my mom and dad,

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:16.610
I don't know a thing about him.

00:04:16.890 --> 00:04:19.120
Huh, really?

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:22.750
If he was a friend of your mom and dad,

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:24.110
you can probably trust him, huh?

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:25.690
Why the hell is that?

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:29.560
They often made puzzles
and played with us, right?

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:32.800
Yeah, and you could never
solve a single one.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:35.910
Their puzzles were too hard!

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:38.230
Holding back on your opponents is rude,

00:04:38.230 --> 00:04:40.130
even if they're children.

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:48.610
They were always serious about puzzles.

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:50.530
Wow, that takes me back!

00:04:50.530 --> 00:04:52.240
That puzzle room in your house...

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:55.220
It was big and filled with puzzles!

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:03.220
This goes here?

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:04.860
All right, got it!

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:08.250
Fine, I'll get it too!

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:10.200
Want me to give you a hint?

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:11.200
I don't need it!

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:16.070
They gave me a feeling for puzzles

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:17.540
that still lives on inside me.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:24.050
Dammit, again?

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:28.930
What is it?

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:43.240
What was that?

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.610
The place where my mom and dad died.

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:48.950
What does this mean?

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:51.020
They're saying to go?

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:53.860
Me, to that place?

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:54.880
Rook!

00:06:03.620 --> 00:06:05.280
Now look here!

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:08.240
Why are you all here?!

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:09.510
Okay, okay!

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:11.720
It's time for some station boxed lunches!

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:14.450
Chopsticks

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:14.470
Who wants the rice and veggies?!

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:15.940
Me!

00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:17.820
I'd like the apple boxed lunch.

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:18.860
Here, and here.

00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:19.760
What about you, Cube?

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:20.980
I'll take the mixed lunch.

00:06:21.510 --> 00:06:23.730
Sorry, everyone, Upperclassman Jikukawa.

00:06:24.130 --> 00:06:27.110
After what we heard, we
couldn't just do nothing.

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:31.010
This rice is delish!

00:06:31.010 --> 00:06:33.580
For you, Gammon, I got
this: The meat lunch!

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:36.020
Moo, moo!

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:38.330
Kaito, you get, ta-daa!

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:39.310
Genius Okudera's
Puzzle Boxed Lunch

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:39.880
A Puzzle Boxed Lunch!

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:42.250
It's not like we're on a field trip.

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:44.160
There could be a trap waitin' for us.

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:46.530
I'm your friend, Kaito!

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:50.560
It's only natural that a friend
wants to stand by his friends.

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:52.420
Say what you want, Kaito,

00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:54.560
but I'm definitely going with you!

00:06:56.150 --> 00:06:57.560
Cubik...

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:00.090
With the principal gone,

00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:03.740
the duty of protecting you students falls to me.

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:05.820
Yeah, sucks to be you.

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:10.330
I, Ana, think going on a
trip with everyone is fun.

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:12.930
Boxed lunches eaten
together are delicious.

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:18.080
Going off somewhere far by
yourself is boring, Kaito.

00:07:19.510 --> 00:07:22.050
It ain't like I'm goin' off to have fun.

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:23.580
I see!

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:25.960
Kaito...

00:07:26.530 --> 00:07:27.680
Going far...

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:43.560
Where are we?

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:18.590
What's this?!

00:08:18.590 --> 00:08:20.180
That puzzle from before!

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:26.580
But this one's way more complicated.

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:28.820
That other one was a replica?

00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:32.050
This feeling... This is...

00:08:32.050 --> 00:08:33.990
A Puzzle of Fools!

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:38.380
So, your mom and dad died
in a Puzzle of Fools?

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:40.740
You're here?

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:43.460
Principal!

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:45.150
So you're unharmed?!

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:47.500
But what are you doing here?

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:02.540
Kaito's mom and dad...

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:04.230
What the hell is this?

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:07.730
Observational record for Kaito Daimon.

00:09:08.530 --> 00:09:09.980
Did he say "observational record"?

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:15.580
May 3: He solves Puzzle No. A-87

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:17.750
in 5 minutes, 14 seconds.

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:19.350
This is far in excess of an adult

00:09:19.350 --> 00:09:22.490
Solver's average time of
8 minutes, 30 seconds.

00:09:22.840 --> 00:09:24.000
Solver?

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:28.780
June 4: He struggles with B-23.

00:09:28.780 --> 00:09:31.000
Are number-based puzzles his weakness?

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:35.530
June 15: He clears B-23.

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:37.090
He found the answer on his own

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:38.510
without waiting for clues from us.

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:41.640
Kaito, this is enough.

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:43.590
We will accelerate the schedule,

00:09:43.590 --> 00:09:46.270
beginning instruction in a special program tomorrow.

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:49.020
This concludes our report.

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:52.810
We shall continue to observe
Kaito Daimon's growth.

00:09:52.810 --> 00:09:55.370
This is Akira Daimon of POG Japan.

00:09:55.370 --> 00:09:56.970
And Shizuka, ditto.

00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:08.600
I..It's gotta be a lie.

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:12.800
I saw it on TV; today's CGI is awesome!

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:14.000
They can make anything!

00:10:14.370 --> 00:10:15.550
POG...

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:19.760
They can make a young actor look old!

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:23.530
My dad and mom were POG?

00:10:23.530 --> 00:10:25.690
O..Oh, and also... Also...

00:10:27.790 --> 00:10:30.150
No! It can't be, Kaito!

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:32.040
It's true.

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:35.150
Those two were POG members.

00:10:36.890 --> 00:10:39.440
Principal, how can you know that?

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:40.730
Kaito,

00:10:40.730 --> 00:10:42.960
you were specially educated and raised

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:45.870
to awaken your Phi-Brain potential.

00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:48.160
M..Mr. Principal!

00:10:48.520 --> 00:10:51.440
Those two were gifted POG Givers

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:54.170
chosen for that purpose.

00:10:54.830 --> 00:10:55.670
You lie.

00:10:56.180 --> 00:10:57.610
They...

00:10:57.610 --> 00:10:59.680
were not your real parents.

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:05.910
No record remains of you from

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:08.990
before you were entrusted to them.

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:11.980
Kaito...

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:14.780
How do you know that?!

00:11:14.780 --> 00:11:15.770
Because...

00:11:16.670 --> 00:11:20.780
I, too, am a POG member.

00:11:25.070 --> 00:11:26.120
It's a lie.

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:29.120
IT'S A LIE!

00:11:30.650 --> 00:11:32.120
Baron Kaidou...

00:11:32.510 --> 00:11:34.510
He has completed his mission.

00:11:35.450 --> 00:11:36.710
Mission?

00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:41.220
He has memories of a father and mother.

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:44.470
But it was a fabrication.

00:11:44.940 --> 00:11:48.510
They were carrying out
their duty, nothing more.

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:52.480
They pretended to be
Kaito Daimon's parents.

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:56.310
And Kaito was told the
truth by Baron Kaidou,

00:11:56.310 --> 00:11:58.600
at the place where his "parents" died.

00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:01.490
B..But Kaito Daimon's "eternity"?

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:05.110
His parents lived on in his heart.

00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:08.130
Even if separated from his comrades,

00:12:08.130 --> 00:12:10.490
so long as memories
of those two remained,

00:12:11.190 --> 00:12:14.500
Kaito Daimon would never be truly alone.

00:12:15.020 --> 00:12:18.000
I shall steal that eternity.

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:23.510
And replace it with a new one.

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:46.970
Kaito...

00:12:46.970 --> 00:12:47.740
Stay back!

00:12:48.130 --> 00:12:50.080
There's something I want you to hear.

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:53.130
You lied to me too, bastard!

00:12:53.130 --> 00:12:55.290
My father, my mother...

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:56.080
They lied!

00:12:56.550 --> 00:12:58.930
Please, just listen.

00:12:58.930 --> 00:13:00.490
I was a tool.

00:13:00.490 --> 00:13:03.090
When all's said and done,
you used me like a tool!

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:04.590
I've had it!

00:13:04.840 --> 00:13:06.090
Screw puzzles!

00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:10.100
Just shut up and listen!

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:16.190
There's no more time.

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:17.860
I've lost.

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:24.360
I can't stop the POG anymore.

00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:27.870
That's why I'm going to
attempt the final resistance.

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:31.330
I will now betray the POG.

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:33.840
No doubt I will soon become a hunted man.

00:13:34.630 --> 00:13:38.300
Before that, I will tell you everything.

00:13:43.700 --> 00:13:44.830
Master Rook!

00:13:44.830 --> 00:13:45.880
Leave him.

00:13:46.310 --> 00:13:50.390
His words cannot reach Kaito,
no matter what they are.

00:13:53.360 --> 00:13:57.170
In addition to being
principal at Root Gakuen,

00:13:57.170 --> 00:14:01.000
I was in charge of a top-secret division
called Section Phi.

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:02.820
Section Phi?

00:14:03.790 --> 00:14:08.770
Yes, a division for raising
the Phi-Brain children.

00:14:08.770 --> 00:14:10.820
Jikukawa is also a member.

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:14.580
Upperclassman Jikukawa is a POG?

00:14:14.990 --> 00:14:16.830
Mr. Principal, what are you...

00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:20.440
Nurture the Phi-Brains,
use their full abilities

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:23.840
to solve the Puzzle of God and
obtain the Book of God.

00:14:24.450 --> 00:14:27.560
That is the ambition of Count Pythagoras.

00:14:27.560 --> 00:14:29.820
Mr. Principal, say no more!

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:32.600
So you were in cahoots
with that guy, huh?

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:35.410
The POG was originally a group

00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:38.390
that created
puzzles suited to the will of the client

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:41.330
and oversaw the sealing
of the prizes within them.

00:14:41.330 --> 00:14:44.620
The POG established Root Gakuen

00:14:44.620 --> 00:14:47.110
to create that kind of Giver.

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:50.070
However, once Count
Pythagoras took control,

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:52.620
everything changed.

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:55.320
So your ass is different?!

00:14:55.320 --> 00:14:56.960
My intention was to act as if

00:14:56.960 --> 00:14:58.630
carrying out the count's orders,

00:14:58.630 --> 00:15:00.820
but obtain the Book of God for myself

00:15:00.820 --> 00:15:04.020
and erase it from this world.

00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:05.880
Erase it?

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:09.230
Throughout history, numerous wars have

00:15:09.230 --> 00:15:12.390
been fought over the Book of God.

00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:15.240
So long as the Book of God exists,

00:15:15.240 --> 00:15:17.300
they shall probably continue.

00:15:17.300 --> 00:15:18.390
In which case...

00:15:18.820 --> 00:15:20.960
But that was why you made

00:15:20.960 --> 00:15:23.710
Kaito challenge the Puzzle of Fools.

00:15:23.710 --> 00:15:26.460
Cube, we don't know it was the
principal who did that!

00:15:26.460 --> 00:15:28.650
At the very least, you didn't
try to stop it, did you?

00:15:29.060 --> 00:15:31.910
Be angry with me all you like;
it can't be helped.

00:15:33.430 --> 00:15:34.930
Along with the risk to one's life,

00:15:34.930 --> 00:15:38.910
the Puzzle of Fools can lead to rapid development.

00:15:38.910 --> 00:15:42.420
However, it creates only tools,
bereft of human emotions.

00:15:42.900 --> 00:15:48.790
I wished to raise Phi-Brains without
using the Puzzle of Fools,

00:15:48.790 --> 00:15:52.380
but the POG's actions wouldn't allow it.

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:55.430
However, your parents
were another matter.

00:15:58.030 --> 00:16:00.070
In violation of the count's orders,

00:16:00.070 --> 00:16:04.440
your parents genuinely
loved you as their own on.

00:16:05.010 --> 00:16:08.050
To speed along your
Phi-Brain development,

00:16:08.050 --> 00:16:10.740
the POG tried to have you
challenge this Puzzle of Fools

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:12.300
when you were still a child.

00:16:13.020 --> 00:16:15.600
But your parents disobeyed that order,

00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:19.910
and instead tried to solve
the puzzle themselves.

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:24.250
To save Kaito?

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:26.170
Yes, however...

00:16:32.840 --> 00:16:35.320
When you noticed halfway through
that this was a puzzle,

00:16:35.320 --> 00:16:38.540
and that your parents' basket would fall,

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:40.260
the count saw promise and

00:16:40.260 --> 00:16:42.660
you were given into my care.

00:16:42.660 --> 00:16:43.680
You lie!

00:16:43.680 --> 00:16:46.020
You expect me to believe something like that?!

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:47.310
I mean, those two...

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:51.750
You should know the answer to that
better than anyone.

00:16:58.510 --> 00:16:59.950
What is that footage?

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:03.080
Look here, Kaito.

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:04.710
<i>Ta-daa!</i>

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:06.200
<i>Wow!</i>

00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:07.430
<i>One, two...</i>

00:17:07.430 --> 00:17:10.960
<i>Kaito, happy birthday!</i>

00:17:16.280 --> 00:17:18.530
<i>Well, let's cut the cake.</i>

00:17:18.530 --> 00:17:21.290
<i>Strawberries! I want a
piece with strawberries!</i>

00:17:21.290 --> 00:17:24.020
<i>Okay, a piece with lots
of strawberries...</i>

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:25.480
<i>Here!</i>

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:29.550
<i>Hey, aren't we goin' to
the puzzle room today?</i>

00:17:29.550 --> 00:17:31.980
<i>Let's play in here today.</i>

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:33.340
<i>More importantly...</i>

00:17:33.340 --> 00:17:34.990
<i>Here, this is your present.</i>

00:17:35.270 --> 00:17:36.910
<i>What the heck is this?</i>

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:38.990
<i>Why would he show him this?</i>

00:17:44.060 --> 00:17:46.650
<i>Wow! Can I open it?</i>

00:17:46.650 --> 00:17:48.500
<i>Sure! Open it, open it!</i>

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:50.410
<i>What could it be?</i>

00:17:52.520 --> 00:17:55.810
<i>Thank you! Dad! Mom!</i>

00:18:00.310 --> 00:18:04.810
I performed a force quit
on Baron Kaidou's computer.

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:06.620
What were those voices right now?

00:18:07.290 --> 00:18:08.980
Was that an act?

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:11.440
Just... Just what was that?

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:17.280
It could be that those two
truly loved Kaito Daimon.

00:18:17.610 --> 00:18:19.160
Love?

00:18:20.290 --> 00:18:23.250
Tell me one more thing: Where is he?

00:18:23.250 --> 00:18:24.290
Where's Jin Makata?!

00:18:24.920 --> 00:18:27.330
The POG have him.

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:28.570
He was...

00:18:29.270 --> 00:18:30.790
a dear friend of mine.

00:18:32.850 --> 00:18:36.050
We would challenge each other at puzzles.

00:18:40.540 --> 00:18:43.180
Like you and Rook would do.

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:55.440
Kaito, don't tell me...

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:03.760
Kaito!

00:19:03.760 --> 00:19:04.700
Kaito!

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:06.390
We have to stop him!

00:19:06.390 --> 00:19:08.390
That's a Puzzle of Fools, right?

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:10.230
We can't stop him.

00:19:11.260 --> 00:19:15.710
Kaito's gone to say goodbye
to his mother and father.

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:25.310
Board the basket, and where
you go is up to fate.

00:19:33.830 --> 00:19:37.010
Each time the basket
reaches a stone platform,

00:19:37.010 --> 00:19:39.270
one flame will go out.

00:19:43.800 --> 00:19:46.230
When all of them are out...

00:19:48.860 --> 00:19:51.280
the basket will fall.

00:19:54.850 --> 00:19:56.640
Extinguish all flames,

00:19:56.640 --> 00:19:58.440
drop all baskets,

00:19:58.440 --> 00:19:59.720
and head for the goal.

00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:02.270
You're incredible, Kaito, but...

00:20:02.270 --> 00:20:03.890
Don't do it, Kaito!

00:20:07.740 --> 00:20:09.440
Wow, he ain't like me...

00:20:09.440 --> 00:20:11.080
The importance of puzzles to him!

00:20:11.680 --> 00:20:14.690
I see, so that's Kaito's answer.

00:20:16.840 --> 00:20:21.070
I will release this
puzzle by my own hands!

00:20:21.720 --> 00:20:24.660
This puzzle that took
my mother and father!

00:20:26.360 --> 00:20:28.970
No, any puzzle.

00:20:29.570 --> 00:20:31.210
It's not the puzzle that's bad.

00:20:32.340 --> 00:20:34.690
The one who betrays you is always
the human who made it.

00:20:34.690 --> 00:20:37.210
Yes, just like Jin said.

00:20:37.860 --> 00:20:39.210
I can hear it.

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:43.110
The truth is, it doesn't
wanna kill people anymore.

00:20:43.110 --> 00:20:45.540
It's telling me it wants to be freed!

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:47.440
So...

00:20:48.470 --> 00:20:50.220
I will solve it!

00:21:22.220 --> 00:21:24.220
He really friggin' solved it.

00:21:35.350 --> 00:21:38.650
The puzzle is saying, "Thank you."

00:21:39.540 --> 00:21:41.560
Dad! Mom!

00:21:43.760 --> 00:21:46.240
Rook, I will solve your puzzles!

00:21:46.790 --> 00:21:49.990
<i>And Jin! I'll save Jin!</i>

00:22:02.180 --> 00:22:05.530
I suppose all we can
do now is trust them.

00:22:08.400 --> 00:22:09.790
That's all right, isn't it...

00:22:10.870 --> 00:22:11.730
Jin?

00:22:16.610 --> 00:22:18.980
You're so far, Kaito...

00:22:37.240 --> 00:22:41.540
Tsukue no ue de umareta sekai
A world born on top of a desk

00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:47.340
Ichiban saki ni kimi ni misetakatta
I wanted to show it to you first of all

00:22:47.770 --> 00:22:52.090
Karappo no heya sotto nukedashite
I sneaked silently out of that empty room

00:22:52.090 --> 00:22:57.210
Hashirihajimeteta
And started running

00:22:58.290 --> 00:23:02.610
Iki hazumasete oka o noboru to
Breathing heavily, I climbed the hill

00:23:02.610 --> 00:23:08.220
Kimi ga saki ni tsuite matte ita ne
And you were already there, waiting

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:13.160
Takusan no hajimete kimi to mitsuketa
There were so many treasures that I first

00:23:13.160 --> 00:23:17.910
Takaramono datta
Discovered with you

00:23:18.410 --> 00:23:24.020
Kanashisa de afureta toki wa
That time when I was overcome with sadness

00:23:24.020 --> 00:23:26.600
Nanimo iwazu ni tada
You said nothing

00:23:26.600 --> 00:23:29.250
Soba ni ite kureta ne
Just stayed there by my side, didn't you?

00:23:29.250 --> 00:23:33.910
Imademo wasurenai yo
Even now, I haven't forgotten

00:23:33.910 --> 00:23:39.180
Mata aou ne, yakusoku o shiyou
Let's meet again, let's make it a promise

00:23:39.180 --> 00:23:44.400
Kei wa shinai, ano hi no sayonara
It won't fade, the "goodbye" of that day

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:50.050
Boku no subete, kimi ga kureta michi
Everything I have, the path you gave me

00:23:50.050 --> 00:23:58.960
Zutto kokoro no naka hikaru yo
Will always shine within my heart

00:24:03.890 --> 00:24:06.630
Looks like we didn't try
to stay friendly, huh?

00:24:06.630 --> 00:24:08.910
Oh jeez, Antoinette?

00:24:08.910 --> 00:24:11.060
You haven't grown up at all.

00:24:11.060 --> 00:24:12.800
Huh? What do you mean?

00:24:12.800 --> 00:24:15.120
I'm sayin' that, like that idiot,

00:24:15.120 --> 00:24:18.520
you don't get what's important.

00:24:18.520 --> 00:24:20.810
Next time, "Rebellion Against the Light"

00:24:19.950 --> 00:24:27.500
Rebellion Against the Light

00:24:20.810 --> 00:24:22.560
What's with that tone?

00:24:22.040 --> 00:24:25.140
You should be a little more humble!
